{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg-3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Sea Keeps Its Own Time\n\nShe rolls in before the light,\na silver breath across the sand,\nand draws her long hem back at night,\nleaving the shore to understand.\n\nShe has no map, no fixed design,\nyet every shell knows her name.\nShe carves the cliffs with patient line\nand writes her mercy in the same.\n\nBeneath the keel, the dark is deep,\nwhere lanterns of the lost drift slow,\nand whales sing lullabies to sleep\nthe restless worlds that never know.\n\nThe gulls cry out their small alarms,\nthe tide returns to take its share,\nand fishermen lift salt-stung arms\nto greet the rising, ancient air.\n\nOh sea, you hold the moon in trust,\nyou break and gather, break again.\nWe come to you as dust to dust,\nand you return us, wave by wave, to men."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_read_input_tokens":8158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"sess-1","uuid":"uuid-151","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:32:26.402Z","request_id":"apireq-3"}
